{"tool_name":"dimelo-seq","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"dimelo-seq","home":"https://github.com/amaslan/dimelo-seq/","license":"MIT","summary":"A long-read, single-molecule method for mapping protein-DNA interactions genome wide.","addition_date":"2022-07-26T07:10:29.149398Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:52:53.502299Z","tool_type":["Workflow"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:dimelo-seq","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Aaron Streets"},{"name":"Nicolas Altemose"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Base-calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3185"},{"term":"Bisulfite mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3186"},{"term":"Peak calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3222"}]}],"name":"DiMeLo-seq","owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41592-022-01475-6","metadata":{"abstract":"Studies of genome regulation routinely use high-throughput DNA sequencing approaches to determine where specific proteins interact with DNA, and they rely on DNA amplification and short-read sequencing, limiting their quantitative application in complex genomic regions. To address these limitations, we developed directed methylation with long-read sequencing (DiMeLo-seq), which uses antibody-tethered enzymes to methylate DNA near a target protein\u2019s binding sites in situ. These exogenous methylation marks are then detected simultaneously with endogenous CpG methylation on unamplified DNA using long-read, single-molecule sequencing technologies. We optimized and benchmarked DiMeLo-seq by mapping chromatin-binding proteins and histone modifications across the human genome. Furthermore, we identified where centromere protein A localizes within highly repetitive regions that were unmappable with short sequencing reads, and we estimated the density of centromere protein A molecules along single chromatin fibers. DiMeLo-seq is a versatile method that provides multimodal, genome-wide information for investigating protein\u2013DNA interactions.","authors":[{"name":"Altemose N."},{"name":"Brown R.R."},{"name":"Detweiler A.M."},{"name":"Maslan A."},{"name":"Miga K.H."},{"name":"Mishra R."},{"name":"Neff N."},{"name":"Smith O.K."},{"name":"Straight A.F."},{"name":"Streets A."},{"name":"Sundararajan K."}],"citationCount":48,"date":"2022-06-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"DiMeLo-seq: a long-read, single-molecule method for mapping protein\u2013DNA interactions genome wide"},"pmcid":"PMC9189060","pmid":"35396487"}],"topic":[{"term":"ChIP-seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3169"},{"term":"DNA binding sites","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3125"},{"term":"DNA polymorphism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2885"},{"term":"Epigenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3173"},{"term":"Protein interactions","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0128"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"DiMeLo-seq","home":"https://bio.tools/dimelo-seq","license":"MIT","summary":"A long-read, single-molecule method for mapping protein-DNA interactions genome wide.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:dimelo-seq/workflow/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":98,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":9,"year":"2022"},{"count":16,"year":"2023"},{"count":22,"year":"2024"},{"count":23,"year":"2026"},{"count":27,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1038/s41592-022-01475-6","pm